{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The issue was in `is_expired` in `repo/cache.py`. Expiry used strict `>` instead of `>=`, so an entry whose age exactly matched the TTL was still treated as fresh for one extra unit of time.\n\nThe docstring already said that `age == ttl` should count as expired; the implementation didn’t match that.\n\n**Change:** `return age > ttl` → `return age >= ttl`\n\nAnything that uses this helper (e.g. `cache_summary` in `repo/rows.py`) will now drop entries as soon as they hit the TTL, not one tick later. All cache tests pass."}]},"session_id":"56ee1710-d9b4-4fe9-850f-f5269c7fd2b7"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":24753,"duration_api_ms":24753,"is_error":false,"result":"Searching the codebase for cache configuration and TTL/stale-entry behavior.\n\n\nFixing expiry logic: entries at exactly the TTL should be expired (`age >= ttl`), not only when `age > ttl`.\n\n\nThe issue was in `is_expired` in `repo/cache.py`. Expiry used strict `>` instead of `>=`, so an entry whose age exactly matched the TTL was still treated as fresh for one extra unit of time.\n\nThe docstring already said that `age == ttl` should count as expired; the implementation didn’t match that.\n\n**Change:** `return age > ttl` → `return age >= ttl`\n\nAnything that uses this helper (e.g. `cache_summary` in `repo/rows.py`) will now drop entries as soon as they hit the TTL, not one tick later. All cache tests pass.","session_id":"56ee1710-d9b4-4fe9-850f-f5269c7fd2b7","request_id":"f3025ccb-662b-46c3-88dc-f249541ef3e2","usage":{"inputTokens":10708,"outputTokens":836,"cacheReadTokens":72672,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
